# Example requests for the VS Code "REST Client" extension (or JetBrains HTTP Client).
# Start the API first: `make run` (in-memory) or `make up` (Docker, with PostgreSQL).

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Create a medication
# @name create
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Paracetamol",
  "dosage": "500 mg",
  "form": "Tablet"
}

### Get it back (uses the id from the previous response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications/{{create.response.body.id}}

### List medications (first page of 2)
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications?limit=2

### Filter by form and name
GET {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications?form=tablet&name=para

### Update it, only if nobody changed it since we read version 1
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications/{{create.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{
  "name": "Paracetamol",
  "dosage": "1 g",
  "form": "tablet"
}

### Same request again: now the version is 2, so this fails with 412
PUT {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications/{{create.response.body.id}}
Content-Type: application/json
If-Match: "1"

{
  "name": "Paracetamol",
  "dosage": "750 mg",
  "form": "tablet"
}

### Validation error: 422 with every invalid field
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "",
  "dosage": "",
  "form": "gummy"
}

### Duplicate: 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "PARACETAMOL",
  "dosage": "1 G",
  "form": "tablet"
}

### Delete it
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/v1/medications/{{create.response.body.id}}

### Probes
GET {{baseUrl}}/healthz

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/readyz
